# Remaining five early-MPI application profiles — prepare only

These ignored tools extend the immutable two-PDM gate. Preparing them does not
build or export firmware. Root owns later run and qualification after review.
No source, SDK, config, Git metadata, original PDM script or original campaign is
modified. The exact committed source checkpoint is
`1190aebce400375c382a5ad54211e2400f98161d`.

The five enabled variants are `esp32-cyd2usb-native-early-mpi-` followed by
`continuous`, `legacy`, `custom-flac-pdm`, `custom-flac-continuous` and
`custom-flac-legacy`. Each starts from its matching committed
`esp32-cyd2usb-native-tls-input-reclaim-` baseline. Only the MPI option may change
from absent to the boolean true. Reclaim, HTTP TX release, selected backend and
vendor/custom codec selection are preserved. Any additional option is rejected.

Scripts and frozen campaign metadata stay under this prep folder. Actual build
paths are the exact short fresh repository paths
`.build/em-sdk-01/{vc,vl,cp,cc,cl}/build`, respectively. Existing build roots,
development outputs and campaign/run/qualification receipts are rejected.
Failure evidence is retained. Neither resume nor overwrite is provided.

Using installed bootstrap Python with `-B -X utf8` and installed PowerShell7:

```text
python -B -X utf8 .build/cyd-early-mpi-backend-prep-01/prepare.py --expected-head 1190aebce400375c382a5ad54211e2400f98161d --powershell <PWSH7_EXE>
python -B -X utf8 .build/cyd-early-mpi-backend-prep-01/run.py --marker-sha256 <PRINTED_MARKER_SHA256>
python -B -X utf8 .build/cyd-early-mpi-backend-prep-01/qualify.py --marker-sha256 <SAME_MARKER_SHA256>
```

`--repository`, `--dependency-root` and `--campaign` may be explicit. Campaigns
must be fresh descendants of this folder. Preparation freezes the existing
exporter's complete clean source snapshot and HEAD before/after, all five
complete committed baseline exports, task/board equivalence to each baseline,
initial seeds, four required MPI README/HOST plus reclaim/HTTP README evidence,
scripts/tools, SDK6 commit/source and the clean SDK5 legacy driver inputs.
Runtime scripts require the immutable marker SHA and recheck bindings before
and after each export and qualification. The original PDM marker
`d0b8632d82f03fae323e0ed631700261c7d7c34488ff9bdae4d1701d5ba00ab7`, scripts,
seeds and frozen payloads are checked read-only; its live build is not touched.
Its exact completed qualification report
`7c2007b1a33a3dfedde6be0ee13e09b463403d6ffdd9d6506fbe1edbbb29a1f4`
and all actual qualified payload/log hashes are also bound during preparation.
The report is copied into the new immutable campaign. Existing CMake object-path
warning blocks are inventoried separately from compiler and environment warnings.

Only each baseline's manifest-bound `app.bin` and `partition-table.bin` may use
Git LFS. Their exact standard pointer, manifest OID, hydrated SHA/size and
already-present local LFS object SHA/size are verified. The pointer is frozen.
All other baseline/evidence bytes must equal raw Git HEAD blobs. No LFS fetch,
custom-storage guessing, downloads, AllowDirty or Setup override is provided.

The later qualifier checks actual Xtensa ELF94, image checksum, OTA capacities,
receipt and seed bindings, exact baseline config delta, canonical whole MPI
module compile and first actual `app_main` call, one ordinary public MPI
acquire/release pair, allocator/free/reclaim pointer and link ownership,
canonical HTTP overlay, metrics DRAM and PDM callback IRAM only for the PDM
profile. The production Vorbis bridge must remain unconnected. The five fresh
images are combined with the successfully qualified original enabled/disabled
vendor PDM pair only after all of that pair's report, image and ELF evidence
hashes remain current. A passing combined report requires all six enabled
vendor/custom × three-backend combinations plus the disabled PDM control.

This remains a linked-image gate. Physical behavior, actual radio pre-app mutex
state and benefit measurements remain open. No RAM, fragmentation or speed
improvement is claimed. Deferred codec extensions and AAC investigation are
excluded. The small pure contract/preflight self-check does not qualify an SDK
application or execute MPI, crypto or network operations.
